// TEST: Bounded Type Violated (aborts)
// The RUNTIME world's half of bound enforcement, and the twin of
// diagnostics/028: the same struct and the same violating value, refused by
// the synthesized guard (TypeCheck.fs synthesizeStructChecks) instead of by
// the static fold. The binding is a plain `let`, so the compile-time world is
// never entered and the check lands in the generated C++ as a guard.
//
// Conjunct numbering matches the static world exactly — `declared @ bounds`,
// 1-based, so `n <= 3` is conjunct 2 in BOTH worlds. That agreement is the
// property worth pinning; the two messages differ only by the "(static, ...)"
// marker.
//
// `max=3` is inclusive, so 4 is the first violating value.
// ABORT: Constraint violation in Small (conjunct 2)
struct Small {
    n: Int<min=0, max=3>
}
let bad = Small { n = 4 }
